+The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`. The same collection is also served in a machine-readable form, a supported surface of the system `[REQ-VET-003]`.
+
+Either surface can be narrowed to the veterinarians holding one named specialty, supplied as an optional filter. The filter matches the whole specialty name and ignores letter case — it is not a prefix and not a free-text search. An absent, empty, or whitespace-only filter leaves the full collection, exactly as the empty owner search returns every owner. A filter naming a specialty no veterinarian holds yields the collection empty rather than an error. On the paged HTML surface the filter narrows the list before it is paged, and moving between pages keeps the filter in force `[REQ-VET-001]`; the machine-readable surface returns the matching veterinarians `[REQ-VET-003]`. Neither surface gains a visible control for the filter in this capability — the filter is carried on the request only.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-001]` given a specialty some veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened filtered by that specialty, then only those veterinarians are listed and moving between pages keeps the filter.
+- `[REQ-VET-001]` given no filter, an empty filter, or a whitespace-only filter, when the directory is opened, then every veterinarian is listed as when unfiltered.
+- `[REQ-VET-001]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when the directory is opened filtered by it, then the directory lists no veterinarian and is shown normally rather than as an error.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the machine-readable surface is requested, then it returns the veterinarians with the specialties each holds.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty some veterinarians hold, when the machine-readable surface is requested filtered by that specialty, then it returns only those veterinarians.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given no filter, an empty filter, or a whitespace-only filter, when the machine-readable surface is requested, then it returns every veterinarian.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when the machine-readable surface is requested filtered by it, then it returns an empty veterinarian collection as a successful response, not an error.
 
